WEBVTT

NOTE StoryCast sample captions for Ten Naira to Yaba. Timed from synthesised narration.

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.397
<v Narrator>Five forty in the morning, and Lagos is already shouting.

2
00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:10.677
<v Narrator>At Oshodi, conductors lean out of yellow buses and sing their destinations like songs.

3
00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:15.070
<v Narrator>Mr. Adewale has worked the Yaba route for thirty-one years.

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:21.134
<v Mr. Adewale>When I started, the fare was ten naira. Now my passengers argue about fifty.

5
00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:26.082
<v Mr. Adewale>But they still smile when I call out their stop. That has never changed.

6
00:00:26.732 --> 00:00:31.666
<v Narrator>Every bus carries a name painted on the back. His reads: God Dey.

7
00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:37.205
<v Narrator>Riders say he remembers every regular, what they carry, and who is running late.

8
00:00:37.855 --> 00:00:43.371
<v Mr. Adewale>A conductor is not only collecting money. I am the one who keeps the bus together.

9
00:00:44.021 --> 00:00:49.368
<v Narrator>As the sun climbs over the Third Mainland Bridge, the horn sounds one more time.

10
00:00:49.668 --> 00:00:53.806
<v Narrator>Yaba, Yaba, Yaba. Next stop, Yaba.
